> fneg(x: i8) = x + u8(0)
  note: mixing i8 and u8: computed as u8
> gneg(x: i8) = x
> show fneg
fneg(x: i8) = u8(x)
  -> u8
> show gneg
gneg(x: i8) = x
  -> i8
> equiv fneg gneg
fneg and gneg are equal on the domain of fneg (exhaustive)
> equiv gneg fneg
gneg and fneg are equal on the domain of gneg (exhaustive)
> const255(x: i8 in -1..-1) = 255
> constm1(x: i8 in -1..-1) = -1
> show const255
const255(x: i8 in -1..-1) = 255
  -> int
> show constm1
constm1(x: i8 in -1..-1) = -1
  -> int
> equiv fneg const255
fneg and const255 differ at 255 points, e.g. x=-128: 128 vs 255
> equiv fneg constm1
fneg and constm1 differ at 255 points, e.g. x=-128: 128 vs 255
> equiv gneg const255
gneg and const255 differ at 255 points, e.g. x=-128: -128 vs -1
> equiv gneg constm1
gneg and constm1 differ at 255 points, e.g. x=-128: -128 vs -1
> a(x: u8) = x
> b(x: u8) = i8(x)
> show a
a(x: u8) = x
  -> u8
> show b
b(x: u8) = i8(x)
  -> i8
> range a
range of a -> u8:
  0..255   (256 distinct values)
  fits in u8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> range b
range of b -> i8:
  -128..127   (256 distinct values)
  fits in i8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> equiv a b
a and b are equal on the domain of a (exhaustive)
> equiv b a
b and a are equal on the domain of b (exhaustive)
